Employee Management API
A simple Node.js REST API built with Express.js to manage employee records. The application supports basic CRUD operations and is containerized using Docker.

Features
Get all employees
Get employee by ID
Add a new employee
Delete an employee
Dockerized application
Lightweight JSON file-based storage
Project Structure
employee-api/
│
├── app.js
├── employees.json
├── package.json
├── Dockerfile
├── .dockerignore
└── README.md
Prerequisites
Make sure the following tools are installed:

Node.js
npm
Docker
Verify installation:

node -v
npm -v
docker --version
Installation
Clone the repository:

git clone https://github.com/your-username/employee-api.git
cd employee-api
Install dependencies:

npm install
Start the application:

npm start
Application will be available at:

http://localhost:3000
API Endpoints
Get All Employees
GET /employees
Example:

curl http://localhost:3000/employees
Response:

[
  {
    "id": 1,
    "name": "Ramesh",
    "department": "DevOps",
    "salary": 70000
  }
]
Get Employee By ID
GET /employees/{id}
Example:

curl http://localhost:3000/employees/1
Add Employee
POST /employees
Example:

curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/employees \
-H "Content-Type: application/json" \
-d '{
"name":"Arjun",
"department":"AWS",
"salary":90000
}'
Delete Employee
DELETE /employees/{id}
Example:

curl -X DELETE http://localhost:3000/employees/1
Running with Docker
Build Docker Image
docker build -t employee-api:v1 .
Verify image:

docker images
Run Docker Container
docker run -d \
--name employee-api \
-p 3000:3000 \
employee-api:v1
Verify container:

docker ps
Access Application
http://localhost:3000/employees
Docker Commands
View Logs
docker logs employee-api
Follow Logs
docker logs -f employee-api
Access Container
docker exec -it employee-api sh
Stop Container
docker stop employee-api
Start Container
docker start employee-api
Remove Container
docker rm -f employee-api
Remove Image
docker rmi employee-api:v1
